{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>To its strength.</b> Lifting its waves toward the place of the splitting — which it had not done since it was split." "<b>And the Egyptians fled toward it.</b> For from the start of the morning watch, the hand of YHWH was upon them to strike them, and then they said, 'Let us flee,' and fled until the turning of morning by way of the split. And at the time of morning's turning, the sea returned to its strength, lifting its waves in the place of the splitting, where the Egyptians had arrived at that very hour — so they were found fleeing toward the sea." "<b>And YHWH shook off the Egyptians.</b> The king and his people — He shook them off from the chariots onto the sea floor, as in חָצְנִי נִעַרְתִּי (Nehemiah 5:13), הִתְנַעֲרִי מֵעָפָר (Isaiah 52:2)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:33.997714864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}